c sequence with a common difference $d=11:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =11 \\\\  & =-3\\,311-(-3\\,322) \\\\  & =-3\\,300-(-3\\,311) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-3\\,322\\,+(n-1)\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =-3\\,322+11n-11 \\\\  & =11n-3\\,333.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={11n-3\\,333:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11N-3\\,333 & =2\\,332 \\\\ 11N & =5\\,665 \\\\ N & =\\frac{5\\,665}{11} \\\\ N & =515\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={11n-3\\,333:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 515}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $515$ elements, we must have $|A|=515.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ab48e01b-c429-5203-be5f-b45cb0385cc3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ab48e01b-c429-5203-be5f-b45cb0385cc3" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab48e01b-c429-5203-be5f-b45cb0385cc3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-72e15f12-6167-53da-861e-1377f406055a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72e15f12-6167-53da-861e-1377f406055a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72e15f12-6167-53da-861e-1377f406055a" :answer/id #uuid "72e15f12-6167-53da-861e-1377f406055a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "515" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287695 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-526a4e40-b433-5ae4-b0d0-076b0cc4ea5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-526a4e40-b433-5ae4-b0d0-076b0cc4ea5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "526a4e40-b433-5ae4-b0d0-076b0cc4ea5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ae43780d-d381-53a3-8d6b-71a453f52f73" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae43780d-d381-53a3-8d6b-71a453f52f73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae43780d-d381-53a3-8d6b-71a453f52f73" :answer/id #uuid "ae43780d-d381-53a3-8d6b-71a453f52f73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,371" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0347061a-970d-5566-8d6a-57e3c30b6fb2" :question/id #uuid "0347061a-970d-5566-8d6a-57e3c30b6fb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-181577" :question/problem "If $A={5,20,80,320,…,5\\,368\\,709\\,120},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n5,\\,20,\\,80,\\,320,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =4 \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{80}{20} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=5({4}^{n-1})=\\frac{5}{4}(4)^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{5}{4}(4)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}(4)^{N} & =5\\,368\\,709\\,120 \\\\ {4}^{N} & =4\\,294\\,967\\,296 \\\\ N & ={log}_{4}⁡(4\\,294\\,967\\,296) \\\\ N & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(4\\,294\\,967\\,296)}{{log}_{10}⁡(4)} \\\\ N & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{5}{4}(4)^{n}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $16$ elements, we must have $|A|=16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-757b53fd-f4bb-5830-9604-cf22f83bd7d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-757b53fd-f4bb-5830-9604-cf22f83bd7d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "757b53fd-f4bb-5830-9604-cf22f83bd7d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d7b2fd89-a660-5176-a690-d8f8260781b3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d7b2fd89-a660-5176-a690-d8f8260781b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7b2fd89-a660-5176-a690-d8f8260781b3" :answer/id #uuid "d7b2fd89-a660-5176-a690-d8f8260781b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9bc860de-458f-50fe-a95e-897939b46d0f" :question/id #uuid "9bc860de-458f-50fe-a95e-897939b46d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181581" :question/problem "If $A={1,5,25,125,…,30\\,517\\,578\\,125},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,5,\\,25,\\,125,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{5} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=1\\cdot {5}^{n-1}={5}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{5}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{N-1} & =30\\,517\\,578\\,125 \\\\ N-1 & ={log}_{5}⁡(30\\,517\\,578\\,125) \\\\ N-1 & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(30\\,517\\,578\\,125)}{{log}_{10}⁡(5)} \\\\ N-1 & =15 \\\\ N & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={{5}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $16$ elements, we must have $|A|=16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6003be51-464a-5fff-b640-c989db581606"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6003be51-464a-5fff-b640-c989db581606" :answer-field/id #uuid "6003be51-464a-5fff-b640-c989db581606" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-393db834-e593-560c-987f-8e69f57279cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-393db834-e593-560c-987f-8e69f57279cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-393db834-e593-560c-987f-8e69f57279cb" :answer/id #uuid "393db834-e593-560c-987f-8e69f57279cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054907 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
